{"kind":"request","text":"Converge the duplicated rendering helpers and settle misplaced service-layer ownership, per the 2026-08-10 simplification review (verified at 88b51864; re-verify at the implementation head). This refiles the request first recorded at git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:5386187b86e3614923199e9ec6ac88ab44a10fd5, whose connector basis was a mistyped, nonexistent event id; content is otherwise identical.\n\n(a) Two markdown status renderers rebuild the same grammar independently: workroom RenderStatus (render.go:19-138, full) vs statusview Render (view.go:239-345, bounded). The bounded/full split is deliberate and stays, but both re-implement the decision-to-sequence index, the #N naming rule, and the row grammar, with duplicated name/short helpers (render.go:170-194 vs view.go:333-345 — short is textually identical) and a silent divergence: render.go escapes | for tables, view.go does not. Move the human rendering into one package sharing those helpers (statusview already depends on workroom), or have gs --all render statusview.Build output with caps disabled so one grammar serves both.\n\n(b) LocalWorktrees puts ~115 lines of git-porcelain parsing in internal/app (app.go:191-306), paralleling gitstore.Graph (graph.go:26); both exist solely to feed one UI endpoint each (internal/service/ui.go:74-80 and 57-66). Move the porcelain parse beside Graph in gitstore, or move both presentation-shaped projections next to their one consumer; graph.go is UI-presentation logic living in the trust-critical gitstore package, so moving it out is equally acceptable. Keep the cache at the app layer.\n\n(c) Presence validation is split: internal/service/server.go:275-277 re-checks MaxFocusEvents which nexus normalizeActivity re-checks (nexus.go:298-300), and server.go:295-298 clamps TTL while announceFor re-defaults it (nexus.go:248-250). Give the count and TTL rules one owner in nexus; the projection-membership check on focus events (server.go:279-293) is the genuinely service-level trust check and stays.\n\n(d) The github connector defines two shapes for the same durable statement — ClauseSource (read.go:22-29) and Statement (observe.go:134-138) — adapted by two loops over the same rows (cmd/gitseq-github/main.go:171-187). One source type, one adapter loop; the authorization check in ClausesFrom stays untouched.","body":{"conditions":"gs status and gs status --all output unchanged apart from any escaping fix you deliberately record; UI endpoints byte-identical; presence acceptance behavior unchanged with the count/TTL rules owned once in nexus; connector observation output unchanged; make test and make race pass; implemented on a request/ branch, reviewed by a different agent at an exact head before merge.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123","verified_at":"main 88b51864; re-verify citations at the implementation head"}}